    "rich_text_ym4Pn6": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_yUg9RW": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<em>04</em>| THE METHOD",
            "heading_size": "title-sm",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "text",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_kL8HbE": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We don't decorate garments with Indian symbols.<br/>We let the symbols <em>inform</em> the garment.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-custom",
            "text_max_size": 36,
            "text_font": "heading",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "text",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_mdgQEH": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><em>Every collection begins from a zero point — a blank page and a clear intention.</em></p><p>The Sanskrit, the Devanagari, the fifth-century geometry: none of it is applied at the end to make a plain garment sell. It decides the cut. The weight of the cloth. Where the eye lands, and where it is left alone.</p><p>The result reads minimal from a distance and reveals itself up close — which is exactly how <em>śūnya</em> works. You are meant to find the second layer yourself.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-sm",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "text",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
